# MOON at /moon-astra/ (added 2026-09-05, web-frontend-lead).
# Placed FIRST so no broader rule added later can shadow the API proxy.
# Rule 1 is a proxy rewrite: /moon-astra/api/v1/observe → upstream /api/v1/observe
# on the persistent world backend (fleet-lead-provisioned, health-verified 200 ok:true).
# Rule 2 serves the entry page with or without a trailing slash.
# Deliberately absent: no /moon-astra → /moon-astra/ redirect (Netlify normalizes
# trailing slashes when matching; an explicit one can loop), and no SPA fallback —
# missing game assets must 404, not silently return index.html.
#
# 🚨 THE API HOST ON THE NEXT LINE IS REWRITTEN PER DEPLOY CONTEXT. Do not assume
# what you read here is what a given deploy serves. This file is the PRODUCTION
# form; deploy-preview and branch-deploy builds rewrite it to the STAGING world
# via the context-scoped build command in netlify.toml. Read that file too.
#
# Why the swap lives in a build command and NOT in netlify.toml redirect rules
# (both halves verified against Netlify's own docs 2026-09-05, not assumed):
#   1. "Rules in the _redirects file are always processed first, followed by
#      rules in the Netlify configuration file." First match wins. So ANY rule
#      here shadows a netlify.toml rule for the same path — a context block in
#      netlify.toml would be dead code while this line stands.
#   2. Deeper, and the reason the obvious fix cannot work at all:
#      "Certain keys, such as [build] and [[plugins]] but not [[redirects]] or
#      [[headers]], allow you to set [context] properties." / "Redirects and
#      headers are GLOBAL for all builds - they do not get scoped to contexts no
#      matter where you define them in the file. For context-specific rules, use
#      _headers or _redirects files, which are PER-DEPLOY."
#      netlify.toml redirects are NOT context-scopable. A per-deploy _redirects
#      file is the documented mechanism, and [build].command IS context-scopable.
#
# Failure mode is FAIL-CLOSED by construction: if the preview build command ever
# stops running, no rule matches /moon-astra/api/* (no other pattern in this file
# does, and there is no SPA fallback), so preview API calls 404 rather than
# silently reaching the production world. A preview must never mutate the real
# shared world; 404 is the safe direction to fail.
/moon-astra/api/*  https://moon-astra-api.ai-civ.com/api/:splat  200!
/moon-astra  /moon-astra/index.html  200

# Proxy HUB API through Netlify to avoid mixed content (HTTPS page → HTTP API)
/hub-api/*  http://87.99.131.49:8900/:splat  200

